that well over 150 car makers operate

235
00:11:55,463 --> 00:11:58,653
in China, and that number is
widely tipped to fall sharply.

236
00:11:58,703 --> 00:12:02,313
It named the likely survivors
as the biggest groups:

237
00:12:02,363 --> 00:12:06,613
BYD, Geely, SAIC, GWM and Chery.

238
00:12:06,663 --> 00:12:08,493
The dealer numbers show why.

239
00:12:08,543 --> 00:12:11,113
BDO reported that in early 2026,

240
00:12:11,163 --> 00:12:14,893
a typical Toyota dealer was
selling around 72 new cars a month.

241
00:12:14,943 --> 00:12:16,953
A BYD dealer, 48.

242
00:12:17,003 --> 00:12:21,033
But some newer Chinese brands were
selling just a handful per dealer Geely

243
00:12:21,083 --> 00:12:23,493
seven, JAC three, Deepal two.

244
00:12:23,543 --> 00:12:25,553
Even the boss of one Chinese brand,

245
00:12:25,603 --> 00:12:29,853
Leapmotor, has admitted that not all
Chinese brands will survive in Australia.

246
00:12:29,903 --> 00:12:31,373
Then there's resale value.

247
00:12:31,423 --> 00:12:33,133
Many of these cars are electric,

248
00:12:33,183 --> 00:12:35,993
and electric cars have
generally lost value faster.

249
00:12:36,043 --> 00:12:41,493
A 2025 Pickles and Datium analysis found
a two-year-old BYD Atto 3 kept about

250
00:12:41,543 --> 00:12:47,113
54 per cent of its value, compared with
about 88 per cent for a Toyota RAV4.

251
00:12:47,163 --> 00:12:50,153
And as we covered in our
video on BYD crash repairs,

252
00:12:50,203 --> 00:12:54,073
parts and approved repairers can be
a real issue for fast-growing brands.

253
00:12:54,123 --> 00:12:55,813
None of that means Chinese cars are bad.

254
00:12:55,863 --> 00:12:59,213
It means you need to choose
the brand, not just the deal.

255
00:12:59,263 --> 00:13:02,413
There's also a bigger-picture
question that some buyers are asking:

256
00:13:02,463 --> 00:13:05,493
what happens if trade
tensions or politics change?

257
00:13:05,543 --> 00:13:07,333
In late October 2026,

258
00:13:07,383 --> 00:13:10,673
the federal government said Australia
would not follow the United States and

259
00:13:10,723 --> 00:13:14,273
other countries in banning
Chinese cars from military sites.

260
00:13:14,323 --> 00:13:17,333
For everyday buyers, there's
no sign of restrictions here.

261
00:13:17,383 --> 00:13:21,313
But it's a reminder that the car market
is now tied up with global politics in

262
00:13:21,363 --> 00:13:22,923
a way it never used to be.

263
00:13:23,631 --> 00:13:26,081
So what are the established
brands doing about it?

264
00:13:26,131 --> 00:13:28,481
Toyota insists it's not in decline.

265
00:13:28,531 --> 00:13:31,501
In October 2026, its
Australian sales boss,

266
00:13:31,551 --> 00:13:35,381
John Pappas, was asked whether Toyota
was preparing for a smaller future.

267
00:13:35,431 --> 00:13:36,981
His answer: "No.

268
00:13:37,031 --> 00:13:38,481
We don't plan to be declining.

269
00:13:38,531 --> 00:13:42,121
We plan to continue to grow." He said
Toyota's order books remain "very,

270
00:13:42,171 --> 00:13:46,501
very healthy", and blamed much of the
2026 drop on supply problems with the

271
00:13:46,551 --> 00:13:48,581
new RAV4 and HiLux.

272
00:13:48,631 --> 00:13:50,421
And the RAV4 is bouncing back.

273
00:13:50,471 --> 00:13:54,081
In September, it was the
second-best-selling vehicle in the country,

274
00:13:54,131 --> 00:13:57,921
with 4,624 sales, up 81 per cent.

275
00:13:57,971 --> 00:14:02,721
Toyota also has a cheaper RAV4
plug-in hybrid coming in 2027,

276
00:14:02,771 --> 00:14:06,001
and it's offering a rare four-thousand-dollar
bonus on the HiLux to fight

277
00:14:06,051 --> 00:14:06,841
back.

278
00:14:06,891 --> 00:14:08,761
Others are cutting prices hard.

279
00:14:08,811 --> 00:14:12,281
Kia slashed up to fifteen thousand
dollars off its Tasman ute.

280
00:14:12,331 --> 00:14:15,621
Ford cut its Ranger plug-in
hybrid by more than ten thousand.

281
00:14:15,671 --> 00:14:17,661
Mazda cut thousands off its big SUVs.

282
00:14:17,711 --> 00:14:21,741
The old guard isn't giving up but
it's being forced to fight on price,

283
00:14:21,791 --> 00:14:25,061
and that's exactly the battlefield
where Chinese brands are strongest.

284
00:14:25,111 --> 00:14:28,981
As Pappas pointed out, there are now
nearly seventy car brands in Australia.

285
00:14:29,031 --> 00:14:32,171
That's a lot of companies chasing a
market that isn't getting any bigger.

286
00:14:32,959 --> 00:14:35,469
So what does the Chinese
takeover mean for you?

287
00:14:35,519 --> 00:14:38,129
If you're buying, it's good news for now.

288
00:14:38,179 --> 00:14:41,629
More competition means sharper
prices, from every brand.

289
00:14:41,679 --> 00:14:43,909
As Auto Expert's John Cadogan put it,

290
00:14:43,959 --> 00:14:46,349
a car maker losing market
share "needs sales",

291
00:14:46,399 --> 00:14:50,189
and "they need your sale more than
they did when demand was booming." His

292
00:14:50,239 --> 00:14:53,149
advice: don't start
from the sticker price.

293
00:14:53,199 --> 00:14:55,969
Use a comparable Chinese
model as your reference point,

294
00:14:56,019 --> 00:14:59,029
make a serious offer, and
be ready to walk away.

295
00:14:59,079 --> 00:15:00,789
If you're considering a Chinese car,

296
00:15:00,839 --> 00:15:03,729
do your homework on the
brand, not just the car.

297
00:15:03,779 --> 00:15:05,289
How long has it been in Australia?

298
00:15:05,339 --> 00:15:08,069
How many dealers and service
centres does it have near you?

299
00:15:08,119 --> 00:15:09,689
How fast can it get parts?

300
00:15:09,739 --> 00:15:11,609
What does the warranty actually cover?

301
00:15:11,659 --> 00:15:14,529
And what will the car be
worth in three or five years?

302
00:15:14,579 --> 00:15:17,389
Stick to brands with real
scale and a real local network,

303
00:15:17,439 --> 00:15:19,629
and you'll massively reduce your risk.

304
00:15:19,679 --> 00:15:22,989
It's also worth checking whether the
brand has a track record of sudden price

305
00:15:23,039 --> 00:15:24,009
cuts.

306
00:15:24,059 --> 00:15:27,449
Several Chinese brands have cut
prices sharply soon after launch.

307
00:15:27,499 --> 00:15:30,769
That's great if you're buying after
the cut but painful if you bought just

308
00:15:30,819 --> 00:15:34,189
before it, because the value of your
car drops the moment the new price is

309
00:15:34,239 --> 00:15:35,269
announced.

310
00:15:35,319 --> 00:15:37,409
Ask the dealer when the
model was last repriced,

311
00:15:37,459 --> 00:15:39,589
and whether an update is due soon.

312
00:15:39,639 --> 00:15:42,969
And if you own a Japanese
or Korean car, don't panic.

313
00:15:43,019 --> 00:15:45,449
These are still huge,
well-supported brands.

314
00:15:45,499 --> 00:15:46,909
But expect more deals,

315
00:15:46,959 --> 00:15:51,059
more price cuts and more pressure on
resale values as competition heats up.

316
00:15:51,764 --> 00:15:54,614
So, did Chinese cars
just take over Australia?

317
00:15:54,664 --> 00:15:56,994
By country of manufacture, yes.

318
00:15:57,044 --> 00:16:00,354
China overtook Japan as Australia's
biggest source of new cars in February

319
00:16:00,404 --> 00:16:01,954
2026.

320
00:16:02,004 --> 00:16:06,214
By September, almost four in ten new
vehicles sold here were built in China,

321
00:16:06,264 --> 00:16:08,534
and four of the top ten
models were Chinese.

322
00:16:08,584 --> 00:16:11,694
BYD is now second only to Toyota.

323
00:16:11,744 --> 00:16:15,994
Geely, Chery and Zeekr are growing
at rates the industry has never seen.

324
00:16:16,044 --> 00:16:17,154
And it's not over.

325
00:16:17,204 --> 00:16:20,774
The Australian Automotive Dealer
Association has forecast that Chinese-made

326
00:16:20,824 --> 00:16:26,054
vehicles could make up 58 per cent of
new cars on Australian roads by 2035.

327
00:16:26,104 --> 00:16:30,654
The number of Chinese models on sale
is set to almost double by 2027.

328
00:16:30,704 --> 00:16:34,434
But this takeover will also have
casualties including some of the Chinese

329
00:16:34,484 --> 00:16:35,774
brands themselves.

330
00:16:35,824 --> 00:16:38,974
And for the biggest brand of all,
the pressure has never been higher.

331
00:16:39,024 --> 00:16:41,374
If this helped, hit like, subscribe,

332
00:16:41,424 --> 00:16:43,854
and share it with someone
who's shopping for a new car.

333
00:16:43,904 --> 00:16:46,374
Tell me in the comments:
Chinese, Japanese,

334
00:16:46,424 --> 00:16:48,194
or something else for your next car?

335
00:16:48,244 --> 00:16:49,594
And in the next video,

336
00:16:49,644 --> 00:16:52,454
we're asking the question every
Australian car fan is thinking:

337
00:16:52,504 --> 00:16:54,534
is Toyota the next Holden?

338
00:16:54,584 --> 00:16:55,384
See you there.
